      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sediment buildup can cause the knocking sound due to the particles bouncing off and colliding with the tank's internal surfaces, creating a rattling noise. Moisture and bacterial growth can also exacerbate sediment, producing a scraping or hitting sound. In this case, the precipitation of minerals and impurities from the water can accumulate at the bottom of the tank, creating noise and resistance as it shifts and settles.",
      "source": "target",
